WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:07.120
I've been covering basically every one of
these corona virus task force press conferences

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.340
live on YouTube, Twitch, Facebook and most
recently livestreaming on Twitter as well.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.990
If you've not been watching them, your mental
state is probably much better than that of

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:23.109
people who have been watching them because
they really are these propaganda explosions.

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:26.660
But I want to highlight two moments that are
just complete microcosms.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:29.110
Absolutely the epitome of what we're dealing
with here.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:35.290
Donald Trump, when asked specific questions
about numbers, ventilators, masks, how long

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.940
this is all going to go on, when and how many
tests are and will be available.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.260
Trump retreats to vague generalities and weird
statements.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.670
And Trump, during one of the weekend press
conferences, was asked about thermometer availability.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.670
Are they available?

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.670
Should they be distributed?

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.920
Should people be buying thermometers?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.620
And Trump instead talked about just how stunning
it is that there are infrared thermometers,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.720
not a very new technology, as you may know,
which can take people's temperatures from

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.330
a few inches away.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.830
This is what we are dealing with.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:13.690
The person in charge right now is surprised
and stunned at infrared thermometers.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.240
This is from my stream over the weekend.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.360
So you'll you'll hear me laughing, which is
what I do to avoid crying because of what's

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.270
going on.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:26.170
And I say I've seen things when Tony mentions
the monitors.

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.700
They aim something that far ahead.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.270
They say this far away, boom.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.510
And they tell you what your temperature is.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.300
I said, I've never seen that before a lot.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.300
I've learned a lot.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.300
It's a.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.300
Go ahead.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.300
Back corner.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:42.870
Trump's takeaway from all this is, hey, infrared
thermometers exist.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:48.310
This guy is operating on a totally different
level than anyone who has any business dealing

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.310
with this crisis.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.970
And I don't mean at a higher level, I mean
it at a lower level.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:57.530
And during the same press conference, Trump
was increasingly tripped up about ventilators.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:03.930
We have about 170000 ventilators in the entire
country now, somewhere between five and many

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.110
more times.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:09.729
That number of ventilators will likely be
needed during this pandemic.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.490
The U.S. has ventilators in a strategic stockpile.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.760
Trump insists we're getting ventilators, we're
getting people ventilators, we're getting

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:17.760
more ventilators.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.760
We're sending them.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.760
Everybody's going to have them.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:20.840
Never tells us when.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.490
Never tells us how many.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:28.330
And Donald Trump here retreated to expressing
shock that, hey, did you know ventilators

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.780
are a machine?

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.250
Not everybody knows that.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.460
Take a look at this horrifying and sad clip.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.030
You know, a ventilator is a machine.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.320
It's a very complex machine.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.120
And to think that we have to order hundreds
of thousands.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.260
Nobody's ever heard of a thing like this.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.680
You know, when we had in the stockpile, we
had thousands in a stockpile, thousands ready

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.680
